# SPEC.md — Grading System (Vəzifə Dərəcələndirmə Sistemi)

> Build target: a hotel job-grading web app that Claude Code can build in about 45 minutes.
> Stack: plain HTML + CSS + JavaScript (ES modules), Firebase Auth (Google) + Firestore.
> No build tools. Deploys to Vercel as a static site.

---

## 1) Purpose and Problem

### Problem
Hotels have 200+ job titles across 15 departments. Job descriptions are kept in Word files.
They are often old, they don't match each other, and grading is done by feel. As a result:
- the same work can get different grades in different departments;
- HR can't defend grade or pay decisions;
- managers don't know what information HR needs;
- there is no single, current report of all positions and grades.

### Purpose
One simple web app where:
1. **Department Managers** fill in a structured job profile (sections 1–11) for each position, choosing from a ready library of hospitality job titles.
2. **HR Evaluators** score each position on **9 factors (1–5)**. The app adds up the scores and recommends a **grade from G1 to G10**. HR then approves the final grade (section 12).
3. **Admins** manage users and roles, load sample data, and export everything to **Excel (.xlsx)**.

### Success looks like
- Every position has a complete job profile in the same format.
- Every grade comes from a visible, repeatable scoring rule.
- HR can download an up-to-date Excel report in one click.
- The whole app works in **Azerbaijani (AZ)** and **English (EN)**.

