## 4) Screens and Elements of Each Screen

All screens share:

- **Header** (white or surface colour, thin bottom border):
  - "GS" monogram and app name "Grading System / Dərəcələndirmə Sistemi";
  - nav links (Dashboard, Positions, Library, Reports, and Admin for admins only);
  - **AZ | EN** toggle, ☀/☾ theme toggle, and a user avatar menu (name, role, Sign out).
- **Mobile (<768px)**: the header collapses to a menu button and nav becomes a slide-in drawer. Main actions sit in a sticky bottom action bar.

**Routing**: hash routes, so no server config is needed.

| # | Route | Screen |
|---|---|---|
| S1 | `#/login` | Login |
| S2 | `#/pending` | Waiting for role |
| S3 | `#/dashboard` | Dashboard |
| S4 | `#/positions` | Positions list |
| S5 | `#/positions/new`, `#/positions/:id/edit` | Job Profile form |
| S6 | `#/positions/:id` | Position detail |
| S7 | `#/positions/:id/evaluate` | Evaluation (HR/Admin) |
| S8 | `#/library` | Job Title Library |
| S9 | `#/reports` | Reports / Excel export |
| S10 | `#/admin/users` | Users & roles (Admin) |

### S1 — Login
- A centred card on a white background with the app name in navy #14376F.
- Tagline: EN "Fair, consistent job grading for hospitality teams" / AZ "Qonaqpərvərlik komandaları üçün ədalətli və vahid vəzifə dərəcələndirməsi".
- Button: **Sign in with Google / Google ilə daxil ol**.
- The AZ/EN toggle and theme toggle sit at the top right.
- Error message area for failed sign-in.

### S2 — Waiting for role
- A card that says: EN "Your account is waiting for role assignment. Please contact the administrator." / AZ "Hesabınız rol təyinatını gözləyir. Zəhmət olmasa, administratorla əlaqə saxlayın."
- Buttons: Sign out, Refresh.

### S3 — Dashboard
- **Stat cards** (4 across on desktop, 2 on tablet, 1 on mobile): Total positions, Submitted, Under evaluation, Approved. Each card shows a big number, a label and a small icon.
- **Grade distribution card**: horizontal bars for G1–G10, made with plain HTML/CSS (no chart library).
- **Recently updated card**: 5 list rows. Each row shows name, job title, department, status badge and grade badge, and opens S6 when clicked.
- **Quick actions**:
  - "New position" (Manager / HR / Admin);
  - "Waiting for my evaluation" (HR / Admin — opens S4 filtered to `submitted`).
- Managers see numbers for their own department only.

### S4 — Positions list
- Top bar:
  - search input;
  - filter dropdowns for Department, Status and Grade;
  - a view toggle (▦ Cards / ☰ List);
  - **New position** button;
  - **Export to Excel** button (Report A with the current filters).
- **Card view**: each card shows
  - employee name (bold) and job title;
  - department, Position ID and job level;
  - status badge and a grade pill (final grade, or "—");
  - "Last updated" date.
  - Clicking a card opens S6.
- **List view (desktop)**: a table with Name, Job Title, Department, Level, Current Grade, Final Grade, Status and Updated. Clicking a column sorts by it. On mobile the list view falls back to compact cards.
- **Empty state**: an illustration-free card with the text "No positions yet / Hələ vəzifə yoxdur" and a "New position" button. Admins also get a "Load sample data" button.

### S5 — Job Profile form
- **Top**:
  - employee fields: Employee code, Full name, Hire date;
  - a progress indicator, e.g. "7 / 11 sections complete".
- **Section cards (accordion)**: sections 1–11, editable by the Manager / HR / Admin, plus section 12 in read-only form showing the scores if any exist. Each card header shows the section number, the bilingual title, and a ✓ when its required fields are filled.
- **Section 1 smart picker**:
  1. Choose a Department (15 options).
  2. Choose a Job Title. The list is filtered by department and is searchable; an "Other (type title)" option is also available.
  3. On selection:
     - Job Level is auto-set from the level rules (section 5D below);
     - Position ID is auto-suggested in the form `POS-{DEPTCODE}-{3 digits}`;
     - if those fields are still empty, Job Purpose and 3 starter Responsibilities are pre-filled from the level template in the current language.
  4. A small info line shows "Suggested grade range: G4–G6".
- **Section 3**: a repeating "Responsibility" sub-card containing all 7 fields, with **+ Add responsibility / + Öhdəlik əlavə et** and a 🗑 remove button. At least 1 responsibility is required.
- **Field types**: textareas auto-grow; Low/Medium/High fields use segmented buttons (chips); Yes/No fields use toggles.
- **Sticky action bar**: Cancel · **Save draft / Qaralamanı saxla** · **Submit for evaluation / Qiymətləndirməyə göndər**.
  - Submit checks the required fields: Job Title, Department, Employee name, Job Purpose (primary purpose), and at least 1 responsibility (task + frequency + level).
  - If something is missing, the app scrolls to the first missing field and shows a toast.
- If the status is `returned`, an amber banner at the top shows the HR comment.

### S6 — Position detail
- **Header card**:
  - name and job title;
  - department · level · Position ID;
  - status badge and a large grade badge.
- Sections 1–12 shown as read-only cards with label/value pairs (two columns on desktop, one on mobile).
- Responsibilities are shown as a list of mini-cards with frequency and level chips.
- **Actions** (shown by role and status): Edit · Evaluate (HR/Admin) · **Export this position (.xlsx)** · Delete (Admin, with a confirm step) · Print (P2).

### S7 — Evaluation (HR / Admin)
- On the left (on top on mobile): a collapsed summary of the job profile with a "View full profile" link.
- **9 factor cards**. Each card shows:
  - the factor name and a one-line description in both languages;
  - 5 tap buttons, **1 to 5**, labelled Very low / Low / Moderate / High / Very high (Çox aşağı / Aşağı / Orta / Yüksək / Çox yüksək).
- **Result card** (sticky):
  - Total score (9–45);
  - **Recommended grade** (auto);
  - Suggested range for this job level;
  - **Final approved grade** selector (G1–G10, defaults to the recommended grade);
  - Evaluator comments;
  - Evaluation date (defaults to today) and Evaluator name (auto, from the signed-in user).
- **Buttons**:
  - **Save scores** — sets the status to `under_evaluation`;
  - **Approve / Təsdiqlə** — needs all 9 scores and a final grade; sets the status to `approved` and copies the final grade into `position.currentGrade` and today's date into `position.lastEvaluationDate`;
  - **Return for changes / Düzəliş üçün qaytar** — needs a comment; sets the status to `returned`.
- If the final grade differs from the recommended grade, the comments field becomes required. Hint: "Explain why the grade differs / Dərəcənin fərqlənmə səbəbini izah edin".

### S8 — Job Title Library
- Search box and a department chips filter.
- One card per department: AZ/EN department name, description, title count, and a list of titles, each with a level chip and a grade range.
- This page is read-only for everyone in the MVP.

### S9 — Reports
Three report cards, each with a short description, filters and an **Export .xlsx** button:
- **A. Grading Summary / Dərəcələndirmə xülasəsi** — filters: department, status, grade.
- **B. Full Job Profiles / Tam vəzifə profilləri** — filters: department, status.
- **C. Single position** — opened from S6, so this card only explains that.

Managers only get data from their own department.

### S10 — Admin → Users
- A list of all users: avatar, name, email, a **Role** dropdown (Admin, HR Evaluator, Department Manager, Pending), a **Department** dropdown (required for Managers), and a last sign-in date.
- Changes save immediately and a toast confirms "Saved / Yadda saxlanıldı".
- An Admin cannot change their own role (this prevents locking themselves out).
- **Load sample data** button, with a confirm step.

### Toasts and dialogs (all screens)
Saved, Submitted, Approved, Returned, Error, and "Are you sure?" confirmations — all bilingual.

