## 5) Data Model (fields and sample data)

### 5A) Firestore collections

| Collection | Document ID | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `users` | Firebase Auth `uid` | Role, department, preferences |
| `employees` | auto ID | One document = one employee in one position: full job profile (sections 1–11) plus evaluation (section 12) |

The job title library, department list, level templates and translations are **static JS files**, not stored in Firestore. This keeps setup simple.

### 5B) `users/{uid}`

```js
{
  uid: "abc123",
  email: "aysel@hotel.az",
  displayName: "Aysel Məmmədova",
  photoURL: "https://...",
  role: "pending",          // "admin" | "hr" | "manager" | "pending"
  departmentId: null,       // e.g. "FO" (required when role = "manager")
  lang: "az",               // "az" | "en"
  theme: "system",          // "light" | "dark" | "system"
  createdAt: Timestamp,
  lastLogin: Timestamp
}
```

**First Admin**: sign in once, then open the Firebase Console → Firestore → `users/{your uid}` and set `role` to `"admin"` by hand. Explain this in the README.

### 5C) `employees/{id}` — all fields

**Shared option lists** (stored as keys; labels come from i18n):
- `freq`: daily | weekly | monthly | occasionally → Daily/Gündəlik, Weekly/Həftəlik, Monthly/Aylıq, Occasionally/Arabir
- `lmh`: low | medium | high → Low/Aşağı, Medium/Orta, High/Yüksək
- `yesno`: true | false → Yes/Bəli, No/Xeyr
