## 6) Design

### Style direction — Hilton-inspired, calm luxury
- Mostly white space, quiet navy and teal accents, thin dividers, and small uppercase letter-spaced section labels.
- Rounded cards (radius 12px) with soft shadows. No heavy gradients.
- **Do not** use Hilton logos, names or trademarks. The look is "inspired by" only. Use a simple "GS" monogram in a navy rounded square.

### Font
```css
/* Hilton Sans is a licensed brand font. If font files are provided, put them in /fonts and load them: */
@font-face { font-family: "Hilton Sans"; src: url("/fonts/HiltonSans-Regular.woff2") format("woff2"); font-weight: 400; font-display: swap; }
@font-face { font-family: "Hilton Sans"; src: url("/fonts/HiltonSans-Bold.woff2") format("woff2"); font-weight: 700; font-display: swap; }
/* Fallback: Inter (Google Fonts) — supports Azerbaijani letters ə ğ ı ö ş ü ç */
--font: "Hilton Sans", "Inter", "Segoe UI", Roboto, Arial, sans-serif;
```
If `/fonts` is empty, the app must still look right with Inter.

### Colour tokens
