## 7) Technology

- **Front end**: plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript ES modules (`<script type="module">`). No frameworks and no build step.
- **Firebase** (v10 modular SDK, loaded from the CDN):
  ```html
  <script type="module">
    import { initializeApp } from "https://www.gstatic.com/firebasejs/10.12.2/firebase-app.js";
    import { getAuth, GoogleAuthProvider, signInWithPopup, onAuthStateChanged, signOut } from "https://www.gstatic.com/firebasejs/10.12.2/firebase-auth.js";
    import { getFirestore, collection, doc, getDoc, getDocs, setDoc, addDoc, updateDoc, deleteDoc, query, where, serverTimestamp } from "https://www.gstatic.com/firebasejs/10.12.2/firebase-firestore.js";
  </script>
  ```
- **Excel**: SheetJS via a script tag, available as the global `XLSX`:
  `<script src="https://cdn.sheetjs.com/xlsx-0.20.3/package/dist/xlsx.full.min.js"></script>`
  Use `XLSX.utils.json_to_sheet`, `XLSX.utils.book_new`, `XLSX.utils.book_append_sheet` and `XLSX.writeFile`.
- **Hosting**: Vercel, as a static site. With hash routing no `vercel.json` rewrites are needed.
- **Google sign-in on mobile**: if the popup is blocked, fall back to `signInWithRedirect`.
- **Avoiding composite indexes**: query `employees` with at most one `where` (departmentId) and sort in the browser.
- **i18n**: `js/i18n.js` exports `{ az: {...}, en: {...} }`.
  - Elements use `data-i18n="key"`, and a `t(key)` helper is used inside JS.
  - The default language is AZ. The choice is saved to `localStorage` and to `users.lang`.
  - Set `<html lang>` to match.
- **Theme**: `data-theme` on `<html>`, saved to `localStorage`.

